# Local Supabase database (supabase start); copy to .env.local, never commit real keys.
# Two forms of DATABASE_URL; use one at a time:
# - postgres, direct on 54322: scripts (ingest_kb.py, embed_kb.py load), tests and
#   local dev. This is the default below.
# - kb_app through the local transaction pooler on 54329, to test the hosted path.
#   The pooler user is <role>.<tenant>; the local tenant is pooler-dev. kb_app is
#   NOLOGIN until LOGIN and a password are set by hand; the password never goes in
#   a file, so set this form in the shell only:
#   postgresql://kb_app.pooler-dev:<password>@127.0.0.1:54329/postgres
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
# Hosted database TLS (lib/db.ts), used only when VERCEL is set. Locally there is
# no TLS to 127.0.0.1 and these rules do not apply.
# - DATABASE_CA_PEM: the Supabase database CA certificate as PEM text (Supabase
#   dashboard, Database settings, SSL Configuration, download the certificate).
#   Paste the whole multi-line PEM, BEGIN and END lines included, into Vercel's
#   environment settings; never under a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name. The server verifies the
#   chain against it and checks the hostname. Missing or not a PEM certificate:
#   every search request is a 500.
# - The hosted DATABASE_URL must have no query string: no sslmode, ssl,
#   sslrootcert or uselibpqcompat. pg lets URL parameters replace the TLS
#   settings, so any parameter makes every search request a 500.
# DATABASE_CA_PEM=
# Next.js telemetry off. .env.local covers next build and the next dev server,
# but the next dev parent process never loads .env files, so also set it in the
# shell: $env:NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1
NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1
# Search modes. Unset means lexical, which is always allowed. EVAL_MODES_ENABLED
# must be exactly "true" to unlock other modes; set it only for eval runs.
# DEFAULT_SEARCH_MODE=lexical
# EVAL_MODES_ENABLED=
# Daily search cap (lib/limits/config.ts), counted in kb_rate_counters. Set
# RATE_LIMIT=off for local dev and eval runs only (an eval run would otherwise
# use up the day's cap). Exactly "off" disables it, and only when VERCEL is
# unset: on Vercel, RATE_LIMIT=off makes every search request a 500.
# RATE_LIMIT=off
# Access gate (lib/gate/cookie.ts). Set ACCESS_GATE=off for local dev and eval
# runs only (run_eval.py sends no cookie). Exactly "off" disables it, and only
# when VERCEL is unset: on Vercel, ACCESS_GATE=off makes every request a 500.
# With the gate on, ACCESS_PASSWORD (at least 20 characters) and
# GATE_COOKIE_SECRET (at least 32 bytes) are required, or it fails closed. Both
# are secrets: set them in Vercel's environment settings, never in a file. No
# value belongs here.
# ACCESS_GATE=off
# OPENAI_API_KEY is used by semantic mode only, server-side. Shell only: set it
# in the shell that runs `npm run dev` for an eval run, never in .env.local or
# any other file, and never under a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name. Start Supabase from a
# different shell that does not have it. No value belongs here.
